Spec: SDDProtocol
Purpose: Define the canonical compact language of SDD.
Rules:
  [P1] Every canonical identifier has exactly one meaning.
  [P2] Unknown identifiers MUST NOT be guessed.
  [P3] Protocol meanings are global and stable.
  [P4] Project conventions MUST NOT redefine protocol identifiers.
  [P5] Compact notation is preferred when unambiguous.
  [P6] Full human explanation belongs in docs.
  [P7] Protocol defines language; skills define engineering knowledge; project defines reality; tasks define work; chains define execution.
  [P8] New identifiers MUST be registered before use.
Resolution: identifier -> protocol -> meaning -> skill/stage/state/relation -> action
